# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored). Step-by-step, with the curl checks: docs/backend-setup.md

# ---- Server-only (used by src/app/api/crowd+api.ts — never shipped to the phone) ----
# The server functions: an anonymous relay for crowd reports (students at the same spot see each other's reports) and the learned baseline it builds from them.
# Without these the route keeps reports in memory (fine for `npx expo start` demos on one Metro server; reset on restart).
# For a deployment, point it at an Upstash Redis (REST API) database: https://console.upstash.com → REST URL + token.
CROWD_STORE_URL=
CROWD_STORE_TOKEN=

# ---- Client settings (EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the app bundle — never put secrets here) ----
# Absolute origin of the deployed crowd route for production builds (development uses the Metro dev server automatically).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CROWD_URL=https://your-deployment.expo.app/api/crowd
# Optional venue directory feed (JSON shaped like assets/data/venues.json). When unset the bundled copy is the source of truth.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_VENUES_URL=https://example.org/nj-study-spots.json
